    "created_at": "2016-09-29T14:55:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-29T14:55:56Z",
    "body": "Basically, what we need to do at some point is formalize \"in parallel\" as a \"parallel event loop\". Then the \"in parallel\" section we have for `SharedWorker` today would run as a task there. That would avoid all race conditions (note that we create the `SharedWorkerGlobalScope` object way before any fetching happens).\n\nIt's not quite as simple as just one \"parallel event loop\" unfortunately. We need many of them and we should keep them however small as we can manage them for potential future benefit. Browsers can always put things in the same event loop if they want to use less threads/processes.\n\nE.g., shared worker allocation is probably one such event loop. Talking to the HTTP cache might be two (credentialed / non-credentialed) or more (if you do other kinds of double-keying), etc.\n\nI don't think we should require fixing that as part of this PR though. This PR presents a substantial improvement over the status quo.\n",
