    "created_at": "2016-09-30T13:11:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-30T13:11:07Z",
    "body": "Yeah, I think once we have a concept of named threads we could have a \"shared worker manager thread\" that basically handles all the bookkeeping in a way that's reasonably deterministic (two processes doing `new SharedWorker()` will of course still race as to who gets there first, but that doesn't matter) and addresses the concern.\n\nI filed #1843 on the follow up work.\n",
